+// small view-locked sprite after DLSS. Flow cannot carry a sprite that moves
+// further than its own size between two real frames - each generated pixel
+// samples the flow at its own position, and no vector there lands on the
+// sprite - so it shows faded at both places. With the gate's record for this
+// pair (smooth_cursor.hlsl) a second, small draw after the composition
+// redoes the pixels around both real frames' cursors: every sample that
+// lands on one frame's cursor is taken from the other frame instead, which
+// removes both stale copies, and the cursor is drawn once more where it is at
+// this synthetic's instant, copied pixel for pixel from the current real
+// frame. The composition itself is untouched.
+// Positions are template-box top-left corners in each frame's own image;
+// view-locked, so the instant's position needs no head-pose mapping, and the
+// previous frame's copy is found in the previous frame's own coordinates, so
+// the head-rotation warp of that frame moves nothing it should not.
+static const uint kCursorTemplateSize = 32;
+static const uint kCursorTemplateTexels = 1024;
+static const uint kCursorCompositeBase = 160;
